# MIR shard worker HIR residency (driver_mir_shard_hir_residency_v1).
#
# A spawned MIR shard worker loads the HIR of every module from the cache and
# holds all of it, bodies included, for its whole life; it then lowers only the
# modules it claims. These specs pin the body-free residency contract:
#
#   1. the arming predicate: only a spawned MIR shard worker with the opt-in
#      flag arms; the link child, the export writer, the fork root, a per-file
#      unit child and a module-scoped child all refuse with a named reason;
#   2. the interface-only projection keeps every declaration the MIR provider
#      channel reads (symbols, signatures, parameter defaults, constants,
#      structs/classes/enums/traits incl. trait default bodies, generic and
#      extern functions) and empties only ordinary function bodies;
#   3. value semantics: a consumer lowers to byte-identical MIR text whether
#      its provider is held full or interface-only;
#   4. the held set: after the claim loop a worker holds full bodies for
#      exactly {entry} + claimed and interface-only HIR for every other module.
